A||N||1||beachbomb||Alignment?(after strut replacement)||||5||
Z||000000||beachbomb||06-02-2001||06:14 PM||||Hey all, i just completed replacing my struts and shocks, i know in the Haynes manual it says that i will need to get an alignment done asap, but when i put the car back on the ground, the rear wheels are way out of alignment(enough where you can just look at the wheels and see they are way out of alignment), is this normal, i already have an appointment for an alignment tomorrow, plmk, thanks..jim||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||06-02-2001||06:30 PM||||Yes it would be normal. Because when you replaced the rear struts the lower two horizontal bolts are how you adjust the camber and it also will affect toe slightly.  You may have noticed that the lower bolt holes in the strut were oval shaped for these adjustments.||||reg||1
